 "decisions": {
  "target_1": "H (J2 with pi 1, cg 6, sk 1) meets every pass-line bound: CPU furnace under 1e-6 at all 21 grids with all three plans (J2 fails 8, 12 and 20 of them, worst 3.6%, 15.7%, 2.1%); closed room 0.015% to 0.048% at g0-g4 (J2 0.12% to 0.39%) and at most 0.15% at the 9 fixed grids; raw-hall RMSE 0.0827 (0.0778 to 0.0883), bias +1.45%; GI 5.19, 5.17, 5.18 ms, +0.25 ms over the J2 control (4.93, 4.93, 5.00), under the 0.5 ms kill line; parity 31 cases, worst 1.4e-4. H becomes the default",
  "F": "meets the furnace and leak bounds but costs 6.20, 6.59, 6.39 ms. The segment fallback fired mostly at entries of buried probes, which nothing reads; with sk, F costs 5.27 ms (Fsk) with the same frame byte for byte",
  "F5": "null: one segment to the top-weight probe fails the CPU furnace with the jit plan (1.16% at r4)",
  "target_2": "null: fd 1 (G) leaves the bias at +1.36% (control +1.33%) and costs 7.4 to 7.6 ms; fd 2 reads +1.51% at 8.18 ms. The renormalisation over kept texels is not where sv 2's brightening comes from",
  "target_3": "null for every candidate: the band's mean signed error stays between +0.195 and +0.205 against the control's +0.203 (under 4% change). Attribution on earlier runs: B0 +0.106, temporal alone +0.113, sv 2 +0.159, jit +0.170, J +0.204: jit and sv 2 each add about half of the band",
  "target_4": "not attempted. H at 4K: 0.0937 (0.0905 to 0.0969), +1.40%, 10.6 ms (screen rays 4.9 ms)",
  "missed_predictions": "F time (predicted 5.0 to 5.6 ms, read 6.2 to 6.6); G bias (predicted at most +0.65%, read +1.36%) and time (predicted 5.3 to 6.0, read 7.4 to 7.6); band for G (predicted at least -25%, read -1%); H's door-room light ratio 0.692 against a predicted 0.7 to 1.0; F's first version failed the jit furnace (coplanar contact); F5 failed the furnace"
 },
